            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. BodyTech is The Vitamin Shoppe's own sports nutrition brand, sold in its stores and on its website, alongside the newer True Athlete line. BodyTech Whey Tech Pro 24 and Whey Protein Isolate are its main protein powders. Some BodyTech products also appear on Amazon through other sellers, but The Vitamin Shoppe is the main place to buy them."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is True Athlete protein third-party tested?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. True Athlete Pure Grass-Fed Whey Protein Isolate is listed on NSF's Certified for Sport registry, and its product page says it is independently tested by third-party labs for purity and potency. It gives 28 g of protein per 35 g scoop, sweetened with stevia, at about $1.93 per 25 g at the list price we saw."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is protein powder cheaper at The Vitamin Shoppe or Amazon?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Name brands are usually cheaper on Amazon, Target or Vitacost. Isopure Zero Carb, for example, costs about $2.75 per 25 g at The Vitamin Shoppe and $2.04 on Vitacost in our database. The Vitamin Shoppe's own BodyTech and True Athlete powders are mostly sold only there, and with Auto Delivery they are competitive with budget brands elsewhere."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does The Vitamin Shoppe have sales on protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
