---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: author.name,
    section: "Protein Powder Rankings",
    tags: [
      "vitamin shoppe protein powder",
      "best vitamin shoppe protein powder",
      "bodytech protein powder",
      "true athlete protein",
      "vitamin shoppe whey protein",
      "protein powder at vitamin shoppe"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{
    text: "See the Cheapest Powders Worth Buying",
    link: "/best-cheap-protein-powder/",
  }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <ArticleHeader kicker={"Buyer's Guide"} badge={"Label-Checked"} author={author} dates={dates} mobileAd={false}>
      <Fragment slot="title">Best Vitamin Shoppe Protein Powder</Fragment>
      What The Vitamin Shoppe stocks, whether its own BodyTech and True Athlete powders are worth buying, and five picks ranked by how much protein you get for your money.
    </ArticleHeader>

    <TableOfContents>
      <a href="#short-answer">The Short Answer</a>
      <a href="#what-it-sells">What It Sells</a>
      <a href="#top-picks">Our Top Picks</a>
      <a href="#house-brands">BodyTech and True Athlete</a>
      <a href="#cost">Cost per 25 g</a>
      <a href="#tested">Third-Party Tested?</a>
      <a href="#save">How to Pay Less</a>
      <a href="#plant-clear">Plant and Clear Options</a>
      <a href="#vs-stores">vs Other Stores</a>
      <a href="#which">Which to Buy</a>
      <a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </TableOfContents>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          The cheapest good protein powder at The Vitamin Shoppe is its own BodyTech Whey Tech Pro 24: 24 g of protein per scoop for about $1.69 per 25 g in the 5 lb tub at the list price we saw on November 23, 2026. The best overall is Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard, NSF Certified for Sport, for only a few cents more per gram. Store prices run higher than supercenters on name brands, so the house brands and the 15 percent Auto Delivery discount are where the value is.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Vitamin Shoppe Protein Powder: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            The best protein powder at The Vitamin Shoppe for most people is Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard 100% Whey, which is NSF Certified for Sport and costs about $1.76 per 25 g of protein in the 5 lb tub. The cheapest with a listed serving count is the store's own BodyTech Whey Tech Pro 24 at about $1.69 per 25 g, or about $1.43 with the 15 percent Auto Delivery discount. The best certified house brand is True Athlete Pure Grass-Fed Whey Isolate, which is on the NSF Certified for Sport registry.
          </p>

          <p>
            Name brands cost more at The Vitamin Shoppe than at supercenters and online. The same Gold Standard flavor works out to $1.44 per 25 g at Target's list price in our database, and Isopure Zero Carb costs $2.04 per 25 g on Vitacost against $2.75 here. So buy the house brands in store, use Auto Delivery when you reorder, and price-check the name brands before you pay shelf price.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Pick</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Protein / serving</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Price (size)</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Cost per 25 g</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Testing</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Gold Standard 100% Whey</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">24 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$124.99 (5 lb)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$1.76</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">NSF Certified for Sport</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">BodyTech Whey Tech Pro 24</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">24 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$114.99 (5 lb)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$1.69</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">None listed</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">BodyTech Whey Protein Isolate</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">25 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$84.99 (3 lb)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$1.81</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">None listed</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">True Athlete Grass-Fed Whey Isolate</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">28 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$64.99 (30 servings)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$1.93</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">NSF Certified for Sport</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Garden of Life SPORT Plant</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$57.99 (19 servings)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$2.54</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">NSF Certified for Sport</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Isopure Zero Carb Unflavored</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">25 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$109.99 (2.55 lb)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$2.75</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">None listed</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="what-it-sells" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. What Protein Powder Does The Vitamin Shoppe Sell?
          </h2>

          <p>
            The Vitamin Shoppe sells a wider range of protein powder than any supermarket or warehouse club: its own BodyTech and True Athlete lines, the big sports brands (Optimum Nutrition, Dymatize, Isopure, MuscleTech, BSN), lifestyle and influencer brands (GHOST, RAW, Jocko Fuel, Clean Simple Eats), and plant and organic brands such as Garden of Life and Orgain. The product pages we read on November 23, 2026, listed Jocko Fuel Pro Series Isolate at $64.99 for 25 servings, RAW Grass Fed Whey Isolate at $74.99 for 25 servings, Clean Simple Eats Grass Fed Whey at $64.99 for 30 servings and Dymatize ISO100 at $69.99 for 20 servings.
          </p>

          <p>
            That breadth is the store's main advantage. You can find isolates, hydrolysates, casein, beef, egg, clear whey and mass gainers on one shelf, and staff can tell you which flavors are in stock. The disadvantage is price. Many of those name-brand tubs cost $2.50 to $3.50 per 25 g of protein at shelf price, well above the $2.26 median for the 104 powders in our <a href="/protein-powder/">label database</a>.
          </p>

          <p>
            Dymatize ISO100 is a good example: $69.99 for 20 servings of 25 g is $3.50 per 25 g at The Vitamin Shoppe, while the 5 lb tub on Vitacost in our database works out to $2.77. If you want a premium isolate, buy the biggest tub online; if you want to pay supermarket prices in this store, buy the house brands.
          </p>

          <p>
            Stock varies by location, and the website and stores do not always carry the same flavors and sizes. The prices in this guide are website list prices; check the store's own price, and whether any in-store promotion applies, before you buy a big tub.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. The Best Protein Powders at The Vitamin Shoppe
          </h2>

          <p>
            Ranked for most buyers. Prices are vitaminshoppe.com list prices for the size and flavor named, read on November 23, 2026, before Auto Delivery or promotions; they vary by store and change often. Label numbers are from the product pages unless noted.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <ProductCard product={product} rank={index + 1} />
          ))}
        </div>

        <div id="house-brands" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Does The Vitamin Shoppe Have Its Own Protein Powder?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Yes, two lines: BodyTech, the long-running budget sports brand, and True Athlete, a cleaner, certification-led line. Both are sold only through The Vitamin Shoppe in its stores and on its site, though some BodyTech products also turn up on Amazon through other sellers. They are the cheapest way to buy protein in the store.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">BodyTech Whey Tech Pro 24</h3>

          <p>
            Whey Tech Pro 24 is a blend of whey isolate and concentrate. Per the product page, a 32 g scoop gives 24 g of protein, 120 calories and 0 g of sugar on the Supplement Facts panel, although the description says 1 g of sugar. It is sweetened with acesulfame potassium and sucralose and includes Aminogen, a protease enzyme, and lactase, the enzyme that breaks down lactose. The page lists it as gluten-free with no artificial colors and shows no third-party certification. At $114.99 for 71 servings it costs about $1.62 a serving, or $1.69 per 25 g of protein.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">BodyTech Whey Protein Isolate</h3>

          <p>
            BodyTech's isolate is leaner: 25 g of protein, 110 calories and 1 g each of carbohydrate and sugar in a 28.89 g scoop, from whey isolate, flavoring, sea salt, potassium chloride, sucralose and sunflower lecithin. At $84.99 for 47 servings in the 3 lb tub it costs about $1.81 per 25 g. The 5 lb tub, at $124.99, should work out nearer $1.60 per 25 g if it holds the same 28.89 g scoops (about 78 by weight; the page did not list a count), which would make it the cheapest protein per gram in the store. Check the servings printed on the tub before you rely on that.
          </p>

