        <div id="tested" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            6. Is Vitamin Shoppe Protein Powder Third-Party Tested?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Some of it is. True Athlete Pure Grass-Fed Whey Isolate, Gold Standard 100% Whey in Double Rich Chocolate and Garden of Life SPORT Plant-Based Protein are all listed as NSF Certified for Sport, the seal that screens every lot for substances banned in sport and checks that the label matches the contents. BodyTech's Whey Tech Pro 24 and Whey Protein Isolate pages show no third-party certification.
          </p>

          <p>
            The True Athlete page also says the product is independently tested by third-party labs for purity and potency, and we confirmed its NSF registry listing. The Vitamin Shoppe also runs a store category for banned-substance-free products, which is a useful starting point, but the label seal and the registry are what count. Certification is specific to a product and often to a flavor, so check the exact tub you are buying on the <a href="https://www.nsfsport.com/certified-products/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">NSF Certified for Sport registry</a>.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you are not tested in sport, the lack of a seal on BodyTech is not a reason to avoid it. It does mean you are trusting the label rather than a lab's confirmation of it. If that matters to you, the 24 cents per 25 g between BodyTech Whey Tech Pro 24 and True Athlete's isolate is a small price for the seal. Our <a href="/best-nsf-certified-protein-powder/">NSF certified protein powder guide</a> lists other certified options.
          </p>

          <p>
            None of the certifications here covers heavy metals. NSF Certified for Sport checks contaminants and label accuracy but is not a lead-limit program, and plant proteins tend to carry more lead than whey on average. If heavy metals are your main worry, see our guide to <a href="/best-protein-powder-without-heavy-metals/">protein powder without heavy metals</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

