          <p>
            If you want one tub and do not want to think about it, buy Gold Standard 100% Whey in a certified flavor such as Double Rich Chocolate. It is NSF Certified for Sport, mixes easily, and costs only a few cents more per gram than the cheapest house brand. If price is all that matters and you are not drug-tested, buy BodyTech Whey Tech Pro 24 on Auto Delivery.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you want a lean isolate, choose between BodyTech Whey Protein Isolate (about $1.81 per 25 g, sucralose, no seal) and True Athlete Pure Grass-Fed Whey Isolate (about $1.93 per 25 g, stevia, NSF Certified for Sport, 28 g a scoop). The True Athlete tub is the better product for most people who care about testing or sweetener type, and the difference is about 12 cents per shake.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you are vegan and need certification, buy Garden of Life SPORT, but price it online first. If you want an unflavored isolate for coffee or cooking, Isopure Zero Carb unflavored is a good product at a poor price here; buy it here only if you need it today. Everyone should avoid paying shelf price for small premium tubs such as 20-serving ISO100, which cost twice as much per gram as the house brands.
          </p>

          <p>
            Anyone with kidney disease, who is pregnant or who takes medication that affects protein metabolism should check with a doctor or registered dietitian before using a protein supplement. Store staff can help with stock and flavors, but they are not a substitute for medical advice.
          </p>
        </div>

